.TH WHISKER 1 "2025" "ChonkOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
whisker \- socket, network and port inspection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whisker
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B whisker
lists listening sockets with their owners, terminates processes bound to a
port, and reports network status. Exit status is 0 on success and 1 on any
error; \fBwatch\fR exits 1 on timeout.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON on stdout instead of a table.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR ports " [\fB\-\-all\fR]"
List listening sockets from /proc/net/{tcp,tcp6,udp,udp6} with owner PID and
process name; each row is tagged exposed, local or interface. \fB\-\-all\fR
includes sockets in other states.
.TP
.BR kill " PORT [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]"
Terminate the processes listening on PORT: SIGTERM by default, SIGKILL with
\fB\-\-force\fR. Asks y/N first unless \fB\-\-yes\fR. PID 1, PID 0, the tool's
own PID and OpenSSH server processes are protected. Exits 1 when no
listener is found or the owner is hidden (try sudo).
.TP
.B net
Report active interfaces and addresses, default gateway, DNS nameservers,
Tailscale backend state, and TCP latency to 1.1.1.1:53 in milliseconds.
.TP
.BR watch " HOST:PORT [\fB\-\-timeout\fR SECONDS] [\fB\-\-interval\fR MS]"
Wait for a TCP connection to HOST:PORT. Defaults: timeout 60 s, interval
500 ms. Exits 0 with {"open":true} when the port opens, 1 with
{"open":false} on timeout.
.SH .local RESOLUTION
The whisker binary is statically linked against musl, so glibc NSS modules
(including mDNS) are unavailable and hostnames under \fB.local\fR cannot be
resolved by the tool itself. \fBnet\fR and \fBwatch\fR detect failed
\fB.local\fR lookups, report this limitation, and suggest using a direct IP
address or the systemd-resolved stub at 127.0.0.53.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
whisker ports
.TP
whisker --json ports --all
.TP
whisker kill 8080
.TP
whisker kill 8080 --yes
.TP
whisker net
.TP
whisker net printer.local
.TP
whisker watch 192.168.1.10:22 --timeout 10
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nap (1),
.BR chonk (1)
